It looked like a hotel.
它看起来就像个酒店。

00:15:52.909 --> 00:15:53.909
It looked good.
效果还不错。

00:15:53.909 --> 00:15:55.750
It worked, but it didn't necessarily look like the most lavish wedding.
能用，但它看起来未必是最奢华的婚礼。

00:15:55.750 --> 00:16:08.244
But yeah, we had to weigh those ideas, although I mean, you know, when I thought of this within this Victoria run is the joke in life among the gorillas, I guess, where Ted falls asleep on the phone with Victoria, right?
不过，是的，我们必须权衡这些想法，尽管我的意思是，你知道的，当我想到维多利亚这条线的时候，我想到了大猩猩之间生活里的那个笑话吧，就是泰德在电话里跟维多利亚睡着了，对吧？

00:16:08.244 --> 00:16:20.738
And I remember thinking, as I was watching it, I was like, oh, it would have been funny, as I was watching it the other day, I would have been funny to cut Ashley on the other end of that call hearing Ted snoring, right?
我记得当时我在看的时候就想，哦，如果能切换到阿什利在电话那一头听到泰德打呼噜，那一定很搞笑，对吧？

00:16:20.738 --> 00:16:21.590
And in Germany.
而且她还在德国。

00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:23.804
And I thought we should have done that.
我当时觉得我们本该那样做。

00:16:23.804 --> 00:16:27.269
And I thought, that would have cost $30,000 that joke, right?
然后我又想，那个笑话得花3万美元吧，对吧？

00:16:27.269 --> 00:16:31.415
We would have had to book Ashley Williams for an episode and pay her fee.
我们得预定阿什利·威廉姆斯出演一集并支付她的片酬。

00:16:31.415 --> 00:16:38.230
We would have to create, I don't know, her apartment in Germany that she's in, or the Culinary Institute she's going in.
我们还得搭建——我不知道——她在德国的公寓，或者她正在上的烹饪学校。

00:16:38.230 --> 00:16:40.681
That would have been a five-figure joke.
那会是一个五位数美元的笑话。

00:16:40.681 --> 00:16:46.503
That would have been tens of thousands of dollars for one joke, and that's why we didn't do it.
一个笑话就要花几万美元，这就是我们没那么做的原因。

00:16:46.503 --> 00:16:48.096
And we were not a big hit.
而且我们当时并不是一个大热剧。

00:16:48.096 --> 00:16:52.938
This was season one later in season five, season six, the show hits indication.
这是第一季，到了第五季、第六季后期，剧集才开始卖播映权。

00:16:52.938 --> 00:17:01.150
And we were like, hey, we want to do this one cutaway that got $25,000, maybe, maybe when you're a hit, now when you're in season one.
那时我们才会说，嘿，我们想要拍这个只需要花25,000美元左右的转场镜头——也许吧，当你火了的时候可以，第一季的时候可不行。

00:17:01.149 --> 00:17:11.509
Well, there's also so much about television, like you, your character could be contracted for seven out of 13, not for all of them.
嗯，电视行业里还有很多这样的事，比如你的角色可能只签了13集里的7集，而不是全部。

00:17:11.509 --> 00:17:22.349
And you go, it's almost like, I think maybe he ended up in all of them later, but I don't know if like Buster was in all of the first 13 of the rest of the development.
然后你会觉得，这有点像——我想他可能最后都演了，但我不知道像巴斯特是不是演了前13集或者后面发展里的全部。

00:17:22.349 --> 00:17:26.950
Because that deal was like a seven out of 13 or 10 out of 13, and people go, Well, why wasn't in Buster in there?
因为那个合同就像是13集里演7集或者10集，然后人们会问，为什么巴斯特没出现在那里面？

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:27.789
It doesn't make sense.
这说不通啊。

00:17:27.789 --> 00:17:28.789
Because there was a deal.
因为有合同在先。

00:17:28.789 --> 00:17:30.710
They made a deal in place, right?
他们当时谈好了一个合同，对吧？

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:32.509
It's a financial reality.
这是一个现实的财务问题。

00:17:32.509 --> 00:17:33.009
And it's true.
确实如此。

00:17:33.009 --> 00:17:38.309
We didn't have Ashley booked for that episode, but wanted to keep Victoria alive just to get to where we've gotten to in this episode.
我们没有为那一集预定阿什利，但为了推进到我们在这一集里的进度，我们需要让维多利亚这个角色继续存在。

00:17:38.309 --> 00:17:43.750
And to get the feeling of long distance, having her not be seen is actually was a good feeling to have there in a way.
而且为了营造异地恋的感觉，让她不露面其实在某种程度上是一种很好的感觉。

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:50.789
It helps the narrative that she becomes a little bit of a fading kind of vision.
这有助于强化叙事，让她变得有点像是一个渐渐模糊的幻影。

00:17:50.789 --> 00:17:51.390
Yes.
是的。

00:17:51.390 --> 00:17:54.390
He even says, Ted says, I don't remember, right?
他甚至说过，泰德说过，我记不清了，对吧？

00:17:54.390 --> 00:17:58.509
In that episode, I don't quite remember her face, which actually felt like a very real thing.
在那一集里，我记不太清她的脸了，这其实感觉是一件很真实的事情。

00:17:58.509 --> 00:18:02.910
Finally, James Schmoesby, who sends a lot of great questions on Instagram.
最后，詹姆斯·施莫斯比（James Schmoesby），他在Instagram上提了很多精彩的问题。

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:04.549
I can't believe that's his last name.
我简直不敢相信这是他的姓氏。

00:18:04.549 --> 00:18:07.470
I can't believe that's one of the oddest.
我简直不敢相信这是最奇怪的姓氏之一。

00:18:07.470 --> 00:18:18.589
James says, as we're closing to the end of season one, back when filming a production took place, were you excited approaching the end of this first season or nervous about the future of the show?
詹姆斯问，随着第一季接近尾声，回想当时拍摄和制作的时候，你们在接近第一季尾声时是对未来感到兴奋，还是对剧集的未来感到焦虑？

00:18:18.589 --> 00:18:22.910
Where were you in your head if you could remember at this time?
如果你们还记得当时的心情，你们心里是怎么想的？

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:24.349
We knew we had a season two.
我们知道我们有第二季。

00:18:24.349 --> 00:18:28.309
I think, didn't we, Josh, or maybe we found out, maybe we found out a little later in season two.
我想，难道我们不知道吗，乔斯？或者也许我们知道了，也许我们在第二季稍微晚一点的时候才发现。

00:18:28.309 --> 00:18:32.970
Maybe I'm, we knew before the end of shooting that we had a season two.
也许我是——我们在拍摄结束前就知道我们有第二季。

00:18:32.970 --> 00:18:36.289
Yeah, it might have been around this time where we got to season two pick up.
是的，可能就是在这个时候，我们得到了第二季的续订。

00:18:36.289 --> 00:18:42.809
I remember you guys would kind of come down a set and it looked like ominous, but you guys didn't seem upset.
我记得你们俩当时会走到片场来，看起来神情严肃，但你们看起来并不沮丧。

00:18:42.809 --> 00:18:49.289
And then you, Pam and Carter would kind of like stand and gather the crew around for just a quick burst, right?
然后你、帕姆和卡特会站在一起，把剧组人员聚拢过来，简单说上几句，对吧？

00:18:49.289 --> 00:18:52.970
And you said, just want to let you know that we are coming back for next season.
然后你们说，只是想让大家知道，我们下一季还要回来。

00:18:52.970 --> 00:18:57.210
You know, it's the best feeling in the world.
你知道，那是世界上最棒的感觉。

00:18:57.210 --> 00:18:59.410
I did that happen by episode 18 or was it right?
那是到第18集时发生的，还是说正好……

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:02.690
Because I don't remember, but somewhere around here, we found that out.
因为我不记得了，但大概在这个时候，我们发现了这一点。

00:19:02.690 --> 00:19:07.990
But did that make us not scared and feel like we were fighting for our lives at all times?
但这难道能让我们不感到害怕，觉得我们无时无刻不在为生存而战吗？

00:19:07.990 --> 00:19:11.549
No, that lasted for years.
不，那种感觉持续了多年。

00:19:11.549 --> 00:19:13.269
And maybe that's a good thing.
也许这也是件好事。

00:19:13.269 --> 00:19:14.109
I don't know.
我不知道。

00:19:14.109 --> 00:19:20.910
Well, some of these euphoric bursts of joy and showbiz are so short-lived.
好吧，这些狂喜和娱乐圈的短暂快乐实在是太短暂了。

00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:26.571
like maybe it'll last till the end of the day and then you're just back to your set point.
就像也许它能持续到一天结束，然后你就回到了你的基准线。

00:19:26.571 --> 00:19:27.325
You're back.
你回去了。

00:19:27.325 --> 00:19:27.825
Yeah.
是的。

00:19:27.825 --> 00:19:31.285
And finally, is Buttercup a real bake shop in New York?
最后，Buttercup 是纽约的一家真正的面包店吗？

00:19:31.285 --> 00:19:33.675
No. That's all we have time for today.
不是。我们今天的时间就到这里。

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:38.369
Well, look, I know we were thinking of Magnolia Bakery, everything and anything, everything about Magnolia Bakery.
好吧，听着，我知道我们当时在想 Magnolia Bakery，关于 Magnolia Bakery 的一切。

00:19:38.369 --> 00:19:40.210
I'm probably a little different, says Brad.
布拉德说，我可能有点不一样。

00:19:41.089 --> 00:19:41.716
Yeah, a little.
对，有点。

00:19:41.716 --> 00:19:42.426
Yeah, I think so.
对，我也这么觉得。

00:19:42.426 --> 00:19:43.136
We're huge print.
我们非常喜欢印刷版。

00:19:43.136 --> 00:19:45.726
There's many Princess Bride references and hymiums throughout.
里面有很多《公主新娘》的梗和《老爸老妈浪漫史》的元素。

00:19:45.726 --> 00:19:49.527
So I think probably we were we were not into that because that is God, that's a good movie.
所以我想我们可能不太喜欢那个，因为天哪，那真是一部好电影。

00:19:49.527 --> 00:19:51.282
God, there's a good cupcakes and Magnolia.
天哪，Magnolia 的纸杯蛋糕真好吃。

00:19:51.282 --> 00:19:53.579
I'm gonna go order some and watch that movie right now.
我现在就要去订购一些，然后看那部电影。

00:19:53.579 --> 00:19:54.289
Thanks everybody!
谢谢大家！

